WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.100
Привет, Датминс Халойн-Рашен.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:09.500
Welcome to привет русский, эписот 45, it's 20 июня 2026 года.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:13.780
I'm Olya, and today we're going to learn some really fun Russian words.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:14.560
Ready?

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.060
Поехали, Датминс, let's go.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:21.440
Today our word of the day is Солнце, Солнце.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.320
It sounds like Soyah-El-Tons.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:29.200
With the stress on the first part and the soft-tsil, like in cats.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.640
This word means sun.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:38.420
Think of solar panels soaking up the sun, because Солнце is the Russian cousin of solar.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.480
Сегодня светит Солнце.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.600
That means today the sun is shining.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.160
Repeat after me, Солнце.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:48.540
Солнце.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:49.660
Грейджог.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.740
Надо твину Солнце, let's add more words that connect to it.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.660
The next word is Дождь.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:58.400
Дождь.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.120
It sounds like до Охц ждих.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.240
And means rain.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.360
It sounds a bit like drizzle.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.620
Both pointing to wet weather.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:08.340
Идёт Дождь.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.140
That means it is raining.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.480
Next comes снег.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:13.440
снег.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:15.220
It sounds like снег.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:16.420
And means snow.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.700
снег starts like snow.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:20.740
So it is easy to remember.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.020
Зимой падает снег.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.780
That means in winter snow falls.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:27.840
Now try ветер.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:28.600
ветер.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:30.960
It sounds like вае тай.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:32.520
And means wind.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.880
ветер sounds like ватором.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.000
But this wind never retires.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:38.900
Сильный ветер дует.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:41.080
That means a strong wind is blowing.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.380
Next we have облака.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.360
Облака.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.340
It sounds like облака.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:47.740
And means cloud.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.820
Облака feels like an obstacle blocking the sun.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:53.980
На небе большое облака.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.080
That means there is a big cloud in the sky.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:59.900
Our next word is неба.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:00.760
неба.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:02.600
It sounds like нуйба.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:03.760
And means sky.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.120
Нуйба раем светнебила.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:07.620
Бослеви мабхай.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:09.480
Неба голубое.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.260
Дат means the sky is blue.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.100
Now we move to temperature words.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.740
Даворт тепло means warm or warmed.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:18.840
тепло.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:21.280
It sounds like тепло.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:22.960
And feels like tapet.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.060
Плезольный ворм.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:25.740
Сегодня тепло.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.900
Дат means it is warm today.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.180
Да opposite is холодно.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:30.960
холодно.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.540
It sounds like ha-lo-dno.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.560
It sounds like chili.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.540
Вот describing cold days.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.540
На улице холодно.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.600
Дат means it is cold outside.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.480
Ласткам жара.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:44.620
Жара.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.700
It sounds like жара.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.260
And means heat or hot weather.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:50.660
Жара.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.520
Sounds like Sahara.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:53.600
Hot hot hot.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.380
Летом бывает жара.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.960
Дат means in some more terraced heat.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.480
Now let's look at a simple grammar idea using this words.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.980
We often start weather sentences with сегодня,

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:06.380
which means today.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:11.360
In Russian, the adjective at the end changes its ending to match the noun.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.440
Сегодня тепло, стейс neutral,

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.940
because it describes the overall day.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:18.620
Сегодня жарко.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.920
Also, стейс neutral for the same rhythm.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:23.720
Неба голубое, шоу с ха голубое,

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:24.780
matches the neutral word,

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:25.680
неба.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:30.020
Unlike English, Russian makes the adjective agree with the noun.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:33.060
This lets you see useful phrases like

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.120
сегодня тепло райтовой.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:37.880
Russian's love talking about the weather

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.400
because their huge country has arctic snow

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.120
in the north and southern heat in other places.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.440
In many cities, people greet each other with

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.780
как погода, which means house the weather

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.240
before saying anything tells.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:53.060
It is a warm way to start a conversation.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:54.680
For fun challenge,

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.420
draw two days' weather and label the sum

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:00.080
clouds or rain without a new Russian words.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.520
Then say each one out loud.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:06.060
If you prefer, step outside or look out the window

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:09.380
and make one sentence in Russian about the weather right now,

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.180
such as, сегодня тепло.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.900
Then repeat it three times.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:16.600
Now here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.120
Want to know a secret about солнце?

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:22.200
Did you know that the Russian word солнце

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.200
and the English word solar

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:27.220
are actually cousins from the same ancient route?

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:30.760
This word began in Proto-Indo-European

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.060
as Soch-Hadi-Valdol.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.560
Moved through ancient Slavic language

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:38.120
and became солнце in Russian,

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.800
while Latin turned it into

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.580
So and later solar.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.660
Be careful, though, because the Russian word

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.980
nieба, sounds a little like niebula,

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:50.860
yet simply means sky, not a space cloud.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.500
Next time you see solar panels,

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:55.920
remember they are cousins with солнце

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.880
because both come from the same shining route.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.700
That connection is your secret shortcut

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.000
to remembering it forever.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:04.700
You did great today.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.460
Say today's words out loud one more time

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:08.460
and they are yours.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.780
Share the show with a friend who wants to learn Russian

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:13.140
and I'll see you next time.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:13.780
Пока!

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:16.540
And if you'd rather watch them listen,

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.320
find us on YouTube at NERA-RU.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.020
Links in the show notes.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:22.900
At that выпуск,

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:24.060
as Wuchens' помощью,

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.780
EE синтеза-голоса.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:28.760
